  "term": "Eldepryl",
  "definition": "Eldepryl is selegiline hydrochloride, a drug with antiparkinsonian effects. It selectively blocks MAO-B mainly in the brain, which raises the activity of neurotransmitters such as catecholamines, serotonin, and dopamine and can improve motor function.",
